   "body": "Implemented on our fork; not deployed to the live gateway.\n\n- [Parameter-list compatibility](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/ad3badd3abe13b4adff86f3fa48fd70c291d416f)\n- [Keep duplicate effort controls aligned through member/classifier overrides and model fitting](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/4f7e63a88592439c79bb43d1309432ad5fce44f3)\n- [Complete branch](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/nvidia-parameters-routing)\n\nThe first patch reuses the existing optional-field retry and recognizes the quoted list in NVIDIA's `Unsupported parameter(s)` message. It removes `reasoning` only when it is an effort-only object exactly equivalent to retained, nonempty `reasoning_effort`. Sole, conflicting or richer reasoning controls remain intact, including after a refusal has been cached.\n\nThe follow-up matters for the reported group: changing the member's effort from high to xhigh used to leave the duplicate alias at high. Proven duplicates now move together through the existing effort helpers, so compatibility can remove the rejected alias while retaining the selected effort. Originally conflicting or richer settings are not rewritten.\n\nThe exact ZCode-style request and NVIDIA response are covered with synthetic upstream servers. Tests demonstrate one changed retry, subsequent compatible requests, preserved reasoning controls, and a member fixed at xhigh. They fail with the relevant fix removed and pass with it. The final effort/optional-field/failover regression selection passes.\n\nThe branch also contains #3636's fallback protection and #3624's UI fix as separate commits. [Validation record](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/blob/055637f4dccc2b9a843a52a5456aab3f41fa64f5/VALIDATION.md): native/Linux/Windows vet and build checks pass; the full Go suite is **not green**. Most failing cases reproduce on unmodified base ef3b9f85; a handover-stream test fails in the full suite but passes isolated on both base and patch, so its suite-order dependency remains unresolved. No live NVIDIA account test or deployment is claimed.",
